course: dictionary
lesson: 7220
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word phosphoric can mean two different things, and the sentence around it tells you which one. In «Fizzy drinks are slightly acidic, because carbon dioxide in water makes a weak acid, and some colas also have phosphoric acid added», the words acid and colas are your clues. Phosphoric is part of a chemical name, so it means containing phosphorus.
explain: Chemistry words often sound strange, but they follow patterns. Phosphorus is a chemical element, and phosphoric acid is one of the acids made with it. Phosphoric acid gives cola its sharp taste. Farmers use fertilisers made from it to help plants grow, and it is also used as a rust remover.
explain: Old books sometimes use a second meaning. Phosphorus can glow in the dark, so phosphoric can mean glowing like phosphorus. This meaning is old and rare, so you will mostly meet it in older texts. When you find a new meaning, check the sentence: does the chemistry fit, or does the glow fit?
fact: Phosphoric means containing phosphorus.
fact: Phosphoric acid is a chemical used in fertilisers, rust remover and some fizzy drinks like cola.
fact: In cola, phosphoric acid gives a sharp taste.
fact: Too much cola can harm your tooth enamel, the hard outer layer of your teeth.
fact: An older, rare meaning of phosphoric is glowing like phosphorus.
exercise: «Fizzy drinks are slightly acidic, because carbon dioxide in water makes a weak acid, and some colas also have phosphoric acid added.» What does phosphoric mean in phosphoric acid? | Cold and icy | Made of glass | Sweet and sugary | *Containing phosphorus
exercise: Farmers use fertilisers made from phosphoric acid. What is the main job of a fertiliser? | To stop plants growing | To clean rust off metal | To make rain fall | *To help plants grow
exercise: «Fizzy drinks are slightly acidic, because carbon dioxide in water makes a weak acid, and some colas also have phosphoric acid added.» Find and copy one word that means a little bit. | colas | carbon | *slightly | water
test: Phosphoric acid can be used as a rust remover. What is a rust remover for? | *To take rust off metal | To paint walls | To make bread rise | To cook eggs
test: Phosphoric acid gives cola a sharp taste. What does sharp taste mean? | Very sweet | Frozen cold | Soft and creamy | *Strong and tangy
exam: In an old book, a writer describes a phosphoric glow over the dark swamp. What does phosphoric mean here? | Loud and noisy | Dark and empty | *Glowing like phosphorus | Very cold and icy
